# Key Features

- 64 Transistor-Level 9T SRAM Cells
- Independent Read Architecture
- Integrated Row & Column Decoders
- Precharge Circuit
- Write Driver
- Transmission Gate Based Column Selection
- Sense Amplifier Assisted Read
- Fully Functional 8×8 SRAM Array
- Designed for Compute-in-Memory (IMC) Extension

---

# Next Stage

After validating the functionality of the complete SRAM array, the next stage of this project extends the array to perform **Compute-in-Memory (IMC)** operations.

Implemented IMC operations include:

- AND
- OR
- NAND
- NOR
- XOR
- XNOR

These Boolean operations form the foundation for implementing arithmetic functions such as **Half Adder**, **Full Adder**, and **Multiply-and-Accumulate (MAC)** directly inside the memory array.
